00:10:25,724 --> 00:10:31,628
[SPEAKER_02]: Longing, aversion, indolence, restlessness, anxiety, doubt.

87
00:10:32,728 --> 00:10:34,249
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's what makes it unwholesome.

88
00:10:34,429 --> 00:10:34,629
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes.

89
00:10:34,770 --> 00:10:39,693
[SPEAKER_02]: Not because, like, this is about dhamma and this other thing is about mundane stuff.

90
00:10:41,033 --> 00:10:42,995
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, this is wholesome and this is unwholesome.

91
00:10:43,635 --> 00:10:47,878
[SPEAKER_02]: It's anything that is underlined by that mental state.

92
00:10:48,038 --> 00:10:50,019
[SPEAKER_02]: Anything that is underlined by a mind that

93
00:10:52,695 --> 00:10:54,316
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that means that, eh...

94
00:11:13,058 --> 00:11:34,114
[SPEAKER_02]: Even the intention that you might state as, I'm doing this because of such and such, like you said, because the weather is nice or something, even that would be underlined, underlain by that level of a hindrance, by the level of your mind pulling you towards something and you giving in to that.

95
00:11:34,955 --> 00:11:39,779
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's what makes it... it doesn't matter what... it might even be like, I don't know,

96
